  "question": "Four Southeast Asian Wikipedias, four different Korean athletes at the top. The question is not who is biggest but why the four lists disagree.",
  "whyNotPhilippines": "Tagalog Wikipedia is too small to measure with — the whole edition draws fewer reads in a year than a single popular article does elsewhere, and Filipino readers largely use the English edition. We do not report a Philippines number rather than report a weak one.",
  "whyThisIsAFloor": "Readers in Southeast Asia also use the English edition, so a language-edition count is a floor on interest in that country, not a measure of it.",
  "cannotAnswer": "Reading an encyclopaedia article is not the same as following a sport. This counts people looking someone up. It cannot say who is liked, only who is looked up.",
  "noArticleIsNotNoInterest": "Of 8,917 Korean athletes on Wikidata, 7,967 have no article in any of these four editions. That is an absence of an article, not an absence of interest, and we do not count it as a zero."
